Here's a basic example of a simple game loop:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int score = 0;
    while (1) {
        printf("Score: %d\n", score);
        scanf("%d", &score);
        if (score < 0) {
            printf("Invalid input\n");
            continue;
        }
        break;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

This prints a score every time the loop runs, and stops when the player enters a negative number. You can add more logic like checking for a valid number or saving high scores.
